         <ab>
            
            
            <persName type="reg">
               <forename>Henry W.</forename> <surname>Glover</surname>
            </persName>
            <persName type="full">H. W. Glover</persName>
            <date type="birth" when="1872-07-05"/>
            <date type="death" when="1958-08-09"/>
            <note type="gender">M</note>
         </ab>
         <div type="bio">
            <p>Bookseller at 114 Leadenhall Street in London from which JJ ordered several books. The son of a builder, Glover worked in clerical jobs before being taken on as a bookseller’s assistant, probably in <name type="person" key="ID_MISSING">William Glaisher</name>’s “remainder and discount” bookshop, High Holborn. In 1904 he married Glaisher’s daughter <name type="person" key="ID_MISSING">Alice</name>, and soon established his own “publishers’ remainders” bookshop in Leadenhall Street. By 1935 he had moved the business to nearby Creechurch Lane; in 1940 he signed a deed of assignment with creditors and appeared to stop trading. He died in 1958, leaving effects of about £1,200. <hi rend="bold">John Simpson</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
